# research.pdl — pre-broker research universe / refresh policy
#
# The research terminal and yahoo-chart widget draw from this data set.
# History is stored as per-symbol daily-close series in
# data/research/<SYMBOL>.csv (one "YYYY-MM-DD,close" row per trading day),
# which is what the chart widget slices by range.

SECTION      | KEY                    | VALUE
-------------------------------------------
META         | piece_id               | research
META         | universe_file          | data/research/universe.txt
META         | universe_size          | 6830
META         | series_dir             | data/research
META         | series_suffix          | .csv
META         | series_header          | date,close
-------------------------------------------
REFRESH      | cadence                | daily
REFRESH      | mode                   | batch-cycle
REFRESH      | batch_size             | 25
REFRESH      | state_file             | data/research/cycle.txt
REFRESH      | wrap                   | yes
-------------------------------------------
RATE         | min_delay_between      | 2
RATE         | unit                   | seconds
RATE         | live_only_delay        | 0
RATE         | simulated_delay        | 0
-------------------------------------------
BACKOFF      | base_delay             | 2
BACKOFF      | max_delay              | 64
BACKOFF      | attempts               | 3
BACKOFF      | doubling               | yes
-------------------------------------------
DATA         | granularity            | daily-close
DATA         | intraday               | no
DATA         | not_to_the_minute      | yes
DATA         | offline_fallback       | deterministic-simulated-quote
DATA         | simulated_marker       | (simulated)
DATA         | dedupe                 | by-date
```

Policy notes:
- **Cadence**: one pass over the universe is spread across a day. Each run
  refreshes `batch_size` symbols (default 25) starting from `cycle.txt`
  `position`, wrapping around, so the full 6830-symbol universe is re-visited
  every ~274 runs and the most recently cycled symbols stay freshest.
- **Rate limit**: live Yahoo requests wait `min_delay_between` seconds between
  symbols so a batch never hammers the endpoint. Simulated (offline) rows use
  no delay.
- **Backoff**: a live fetch that fails is retried up to `attempts` times,
  doubling the wait (`base_delay * 2^attempt`) up to `max_delay` seconds before
  giving up for the run; the symbol still receives a deterministic simulated
  quote so the series never gaps.
- **History**: daily closes only (not to-the-minute). When a series has no data
  yet (offline first run), the chart op backfills a deterministic synthetic
  10-year daily series so a chart always renders.
